{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you","id":991835,"title":"Making Appearance Work for You","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T07:03:31-07:00","id":991835,"title":"Making Appearance Work for You","content":"By all accounts, Appearance is a rather worthless Attribute, but it really should not be worthless because it reflects beauty, poise, vocal quality, etc. It is scientifically proven that more attractive people are given more respect by their peers, are paid more than their peers, and generally have easier and better lives than their peers. Given the conflict between real life and WoD, how do we make WoD more plausible?<br /> <br /> One thing that I have done is to allow Appearance to modify the difficulty of any Social Test, mundane or magical. Appearance 0 gives +2 difficulty, 1 +1, 2 +0, 3 -1, 4 -2, 5 -3, etc. I have found that it makes it worthwhile for players to purchase Appearance. What are your suggestions on how to make Appearance work for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:42:09-07:00","id":991901,"title":"","content":"That's going to throw the math off ferociously. Just have people roll it more often, particularly with Leadership, for leaders-by-example. It's not hard to figure out where it should be paired with an Ability, but the existing systems examples went sideways or weren't built at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:06:09-07:00","id":991913,"title":"","content":"I've found that having players role their appearance at the beginning of the scene and adding the successes to any social role works. An attractive enough person will still have an easier time, but there can still be bad nights when you get no benefit(failure) and horrible nights where something comes by to make you less approachable(botching).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:24:19-07:00","id":991945,"title":"","content":"In addition to the passive effect, we usually roll it for various situations (usually, the ST does it without the players knowledge).<br /> <br /> (App + expression) (app + etiquette) (app + masquerade) (app + seduction) (app + performance) etc...certain powers like Presence, Yang Prana, Obligation etc can add dice or alter the effect. The roll can be contested between players/characters.<br /> <br /> The effect can vary from getting attention, changing the impression some people have about you, changing the disposition of people around you, distraction...Naturally, this is not always positive, and someone can find herself attracting too much attention, being overestimated, wrong impression or brewing jealousy etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:07:07-07:00","id":991975,"title":"","content":"I never liked Appearance as an Attribute anyway, so I'm just glad they made Presence took its place in CoD and kind of live with it when I play WoD. It is just one broken piece in a broken system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:43:31-07:00","id":992156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(app + seduction)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Urgh secondary abilities that are supposed to fill in for three Abilities on exactly one task.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=991975#post991975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked Appearance as an Attribute anyway, so I'm just glad they made Presence took its place in CoD and kind of live with it when I play WoD. It is just one broken piece in a broken system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Presence has a suspiciously similar description, and you lose dots of it if you get disfigured, at least according to one source I can't recall off the top of my head, so the only thing that really happened was that they changed the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-24-2016, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:18:01-07:00","id":992201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Presence is your character\u2019s assertiveness, gravitas, and raw appeal. It gives your character a strong bearing that changes moods and minds </div> </div> </div>From Vampire: The Requiem. That doesn't really read to me as similar to Appearance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:28:02-07:00","id":992208,"title":"","content":"It might not read similar to Appearance but that's pretty much the way I use Appearance in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:31:09-07:00","id":992211,"title":"","content":"As assertiveness? Gravitas? Bearing? These can all easily be covered by Charisma. <i>Maybe</i> raw appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:41:45-07:00","id":992215,"title":"","content":"Sure, but Charisma to me is more of an active stat, it shows how charismatic you can be when you talk or something to that effect. Appearance is your character's passive appeal, and it affects a lot more than just your physical attractiveness, it affects the grace with which you move, your posture and bearing and so on. So whenever you try to convey a message through body language I would use Appearance instead of Charisma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:36:49-07:00","id":992246,"title":"","content":"A character of high Presence in CoD can be ugly as hell, and there are some official examples of such. By the way, no character that becomes bestial looses Presence.<br /> <br /> It does have a similar description, to some degree, because it does cover a similar function in the game. But it works way better.<br /> <br /> But in WoD it isn't simply a question of using Appearance as Presence, precisely because there is Charisma already, something with also a similar function. In the end, most of the tasks that could be reasonably put forth for Appearance end up being rolled with Charisma, because we hardly see those things affecting distinct tasks, and Appearance does have that feeling of a passive effect, so its something that you hardly roll.<br /> <br /> The point isn't that appearance, with lowcase a, isn't relevant for the game. But that as an Attribute, given how Attributes should work in the game, it does a very poor job. You have to invest a lot of points just to make your character appealing, something a lot of players want to do, but have so few game effects compared to any other Attribute, and those it does have seem to work in a weird way, not adding to rolls like an Attribute should by the rule.<br /> <br /> CoD works it making low-case appearance into a Merit, something easy to translate to WoD. The problem, though, is the hole it creates in the Social Attributes, and the issues that bringing Composure to the WoD would create.<br /> <br /> Sincerely, if I delve too much in this problem I'll simply make the system ever more symilar to CoD, for very few benefits unless I make an almost complete conversion. That's why I prefer to simply play CoD or, when I want to play WoD, I just don't bother much correcting stuff anymore. It IS a mess of a system, and Appearance isn't the worst of it, by far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T23:21:33-07:00","id":992275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristviljan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=992215#post992215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but Charisma to me is more of an active stat, it shows how charismatic you can be when you talk or something to that effect. Appearance is your character's passive appeal, and it affects a lot more than just your physical attractiveness, it affects the grace with which you move, your posture and bearing and so on. So whenever you try to convey a message through body language I would use Appearance instead of Charisma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted and Adventure! both share a good idea on that point. It also prevents Nosferatu from gaming their Social Attributes so that they only have to pay for two out of three!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:48:35-07:00","id":992381,"title":"","content":"Yes, Nosferatu are supposed to suffer from their lack of Appearance. I am curious though, how would you use masks, which have been historically used to protect disfigured people from the cruelty of their peers, in place of Appearance? I would suggest allowing a mask to give an individual Appearance 1 (Appearance 2 if the mask is a true work of art).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:40:00-07:00","id":992669,"title":"","content":"I'd probably allow it, but if it's on a Nos then the Nos in question would have to wear quite a lot of clothing to conceal all of his disfigurations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:16:23-07:00","id":992975,"title":"","content":"Charisma also requires some time. If you have seconds to convince that police officer not to write you up and give you that fine, it'll fall on Appearance. Appearance also caps social rolls with people who don't know you when making a first impression too, I think?<br /> <br /> If you really want to boost Appearance, you could allow any character to take it as the number of auto successes a character can take in any social encounter that relies on first impressions. Or it could be used to calculate initiative for social combat (maybe combining Appearance + Status).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:02:33-07:00","id":993053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=992975#post992975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charisma also requires some time. If you have seconds to convince that police officer not to write you up and give you that fine, it'll fall on Appearance. Appearance also caps social rolls with people who don't know you when making a first impression too, I think?<br /> <br /> If you really want to boost Appearance, you could allow any character to take it as the number of auto successes a character can take in any social encounter that relies on first impressions. Or it could be used to calculate initiative for <b>social combat</b> (maybe combining Appearance + Status).</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I was hoping to never hear those two words together, ever again, once EX3 came out...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:11:51-07:00","id":993061,"title":"","content":"The term social combat is something that I tend to avoid myself because, quite frankly, combat is a physical thing. <i>Social conflict</i> is a much better (and more accurate) term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:51:59-07:00","id":993148,"title":"","content":"Semantics. Social combat (or conflict) is great for those players who can't or don't enjoy roleplaying social stuff. It's also a great way to avoid the moral quandary and psychological soiling of, say, roleplaying a presidential debate between Hillary and Trump. Just abstract the damn thing and be done with it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, mental combat (or conflict) could be used when you really don't want to roleplay a torture scene or the hours involved in defeating a self-aware computer program called Jeeves.<br /> <br /> Optional rules, of course, and easily represented by a single Attribute + Ability roll, but so is physical combat if we're being honest (roll Dexterity + Brawl/Melee/Firearms in a contested roll and abstract the rest).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:02:58-07:00","id":993153,"title":"","content":"I do not abstract the roll because I believe that the point of roleplaying is playing the role. If someone wants to play a social character in my games, I expect them to act things out and then I modify their roll based on the quality of their roleplaying. I do the same thing for mental conflicts or physical conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:13:23-07:00","id":993245,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with abstracting the damn thing, nor with not doing it.<br /> <br /> That said, the rules are <u><b>meant for abstraction</b></u>, so they're only a guide when you're <u>not</u> abstracting. So...<br /> <br /> By my side, when I'm not on the mood for abstracting the social conflicts, I just take the sheet as a guide and let the players talk. Then I just react to their efforts as the NPC would. It works wonderfully well, and then any mechanical problems with Appearance are just gone.<br /> <br /> For the record, I do both styles a lot. When abstracting things, you're going for a lot of trouble to make Appearance work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T06:26:28-07:00","id":993465,"title":"","content":"You know, I was thinking about this topic just the other day. And yes, I did think that Appearance ought to be utilized more in games.<br /> <br /> Probably the biggest problem is that the games never really tell Storytellers when to roll it (or which Ability or other Trait to roll it with), save for a few exceptions. I know that V20 used it as the first part of its three standard stages of Seduction (not having a dedicated Ability for it), the other two stages requiring Charisma and Manipulation in turn. But the idea of first impressions is otherwise not handled altogether well.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of gaining extra successes from the Appearance roll for subsequent social rolls. I also like the idea of treating Appearance as the passive counterpart to Charisma's more active component. A character who walks into a crowded room, and wants to make an impression on someone standing on the other side, might not get a chance to talk to that person (and therefore use Charisma). Naturally Appearance would become the active part of this interaction.<br /> <br /> Something I also toyed with was the idea of combining Appearance with Intimidation. Partly this is justified by the character dressing and standing in an intimidating manner, and partly because more beautiful people naturally hold greater social power, and other people know this. So when a prom queen walks into the lunch room (with or without her girls flanking her), her very presence exerts social pressure on everything else. It makes those uncommitted to interacting with her rather not, and makes those who do to assume a position of deference.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a tough-looking dude who walks into a bar - whether he's personally handsome or just striking in his toughness - exerts his own brand of social pressure, mixed with the more primal pressure of raw, alpha magnetism. Those who are similarly tough will interact with him as an equal. Those who are weak will defer out of fear. And those indifferent or uninvolved will prefer to keep a wide berth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:04:59-07:00","id":993496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=993465#post993465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was thinking about this topic just the other day. And yes, I did think that Appearance ought to be utilized more in games.<br /> <br /> Probably the biggest problem is that the games never really tell Storytellers when to roll it (or which Ability or other Trait to roll it with), save for a few exceptions. I know that V20 used it as the first part of its three standard stages of Seduction (not having a dedicated Ability for it), the other two stages requiring Charisma and Manipulation in turn. But the idea of first impressions is otherwise not handled altogether well.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of gaining extra successes from the Appearance roll for subsequent social rolls. I also like the idea of treating Appearance as the passive counterpart to Charisma's more active component. A character who walks into a crowded room, and wants to make an impression on someone standing on the other side, might not get a chance to talk to that person (and therefore use Charisma). Naturally Appearance would become the active part of this interaction.<br /> <br /> Something I also toyed with was the idea of combining Appearance with Intimidation. Partly this is justified by the character dressing and standing in an intimidating manner, and partly because more beautiful people naturally hold greater social power, and other people know this. So when a prom queen walks into the lunch room (with or without her girls flanking her), her very presence exerts social pressure on everything else. It makes those uncommitted to interacting with her rather not, and makes those who do to assume a position of deference.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a tough-looking dude who walks into a bar - whether he's personally handsome or just striking in his toughness - exerts his own brand of social pressure, mixed with the more primal pressure of raw, alpha magnetism. Those who are similarly tough will interact with him as an equal. Those who are weak will defer out of fear. And those indifferent or uninvolved will prefer to keep a wide berth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with this last suggestion is that all big bruisers should then have high Appearance, regardless of how ugly they are. The stat becomes more about presence and bearing than beauty. <br /> <br /> This makes sense, but the ugly clans would have to take a social penalty instead of an Appearance cap and every character would need a specialty in Appearance like with Arts or Crafts (Bruiser, Beauty, Horror, etc), and this would limit what Appearance could be used for organically (so Horrors might use their Appearance 5 to scare the shit out of you, but they couldn't use it to seduce you). <br /> <br /> Appearance would still indicate who goes first in social interaction, however, as a terrifying bruiser or an imposing beauty queen both get your attention and people naturally defer to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:51:41-07:00","id":993805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=993465#post993465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was thinking about this topic just the other day. And yes, I did think that Appearance ought to be utilized more in games.<br /> <br /> Probably the biggest problem is that the games never really tell Storytellers when to roll it (or which Ability or other Trait to roll it with), save for a few exceptions. I know that V20 used it as the first part of its three standard stages of Seduction (not having a dedicated Ability for it), the other two stages requiring Charisma and Manipulation in turn. But the idea of first impressions is otherwise not handled altogether well.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of gaining extra successes from the Appearance roll for subsequent social rolls. I also like the idea of treating Appearance as the passive counterpart to Charisma's more active component. A character who walks into a crowded room, and wants to make an impression on someone standing on the other side, might not get a chance to talk to that person (and therefore use Charisma). Naturally Appearance would become the active part of this interaction.<br /> <br /> Something I also toyed with was the idea of combining Appearance with Intimidation. Partly this is justified by the character dressing and standing in an intimidating manner, and partly because more beautiful people naturally hold greater social power, and other people know this. So when a prom queen walks into the lunch room (with or without her girls flanking her), her very presence exerts social pressure on everything else. It makes those uncommitted to interacting with her rather not, and makes those who do to assume a position of deference.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a tough-looking dude who walks into a bar - whether he's personally handsome or just striking in his toughness - exerts his own brand of social pressure, mixed with the more primal pressure of raw, alpha magnetism. Those who are similarly tough will interact with him as an equal. Those who are weak will defer out of fear. And those indifferent or uninvolved will prefer to keep a wide berth.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two problems. First, you again goes further apart from Appearance original conception and walks into Presence's territory, and that begs the question: what makes it distinct from Charisma? What kind of proposed action can't be reasonably played out with Charisma? By myself, I pretty much see Charisma playing the role on almost all proposed actions and making it without raising a fifth of the problems <b>adambeyoncelowe</b> pointed out.<br /> <br /> Second, you add a lot of mechanics strange to Attributes, still the very same problems. The game works every Attribute in the same basic ways. You roll them with an Ability to accomplish something. If they're used to resist something, they subtract from another roll. But they are enough by themselves. They can be rolled to add dice to another character's dice pool, but they don't have this as their <i>raison d'etre</i>.<br /> <br /> Maybe instead of creating complicated rules for Appearance affecting the actions that already exist, you could create &quot;new&quot; actions for either Appearance or Charisma? The first thing I can suggest is that you always use Appearance at a social roll until the target decides to look further. Then you start to roll with Charisma instead. So Appearance can be the ultimate roll for &quot;shallow&quot; people, while people that always over-analyze maybe will make you use Charisma since the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:59:48-07:00","id":993852,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Appearance should work as a social resistance since it is passive. Attractive people tend to be socially dominant and that could be interpreted as being more resistant to external social influence (either the brute force of Charisma or the wily nature of Manipulation). Of course, that means that Nosferatu would truly suffer from a disadvantage, as they would lack nature resistance to social manipulation (they would be forced to avoid it by using Manipulation). Just a thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T22:51:29-07:00","id":993905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=993852#post993852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Appearance should work as a social resistance since it is passive. Attractive people tend to be socially dominant and that could be interpreted as being more resistant to external social influence (either the brute force of Charisma or the wily nature of Manipulation). Of course, that means that Nosferatu would truly suffer from a disadvantage, as they would lack nature resistance to social manipulation (they would be forced to avoid it by using Manipulation). Just a thought...</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about WoD Attribute concepts and not CoD ones, so there's no need to try and funnel the Attributes into categories like that. Especially since one can make a case for &quot;social resistance&quot; being in Wits as it is in EX3, and not to be found among Social Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T23:07:09-07:00","id":993909,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a><br /> I used to think that abstracting social interactions with dice was bad. But having thought about it more, that philosophy doesn't seem to serve the purpose of roleplaying. If someone is playing a charismatic character they should do their utmost to get that across--but the stat gives them leeway. Same with Manipulation. If they are constantly falling short then maybe they should reconsider playing that type of character, but if they're really trying maybe they just need more practice. It seems a little silly to punish a player for not possessing an attribute to the same degree as their character. There are tons of actual professional actors who aren't geniuses, for example, but who have nonetheless been paid very large amounts of money to play geniuses. It's important for characters with <i>low</i> mental or social traits to portray those as well. In my Exalted group there's a guy who plays someone with a 1 Intelligence, but he doesn't really avoid using his actual intellect to solve problems. It's annoying--it makes it seem like he just put down Intelligence as a dump stat (which he almost certainly did). The Attribute, not inherent player abilities, should inform the roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:00:51-07:00","id":993953,"title":"","content":"Here's another option: make Appearance a Background. It doesn't get used much, and charging Attribute costs for it seems unfair as a result. Then give it two main functions: First Impressions and Infatuation.<br /> <br /> First Impressions:<br /> You roll Appearance in appropriate social situations (usually when introducing yourself to a new person), and each success adds a dice to all subsequent social interactions with that person for the remainder of the story. These extra dice can be lost through social faux pas or dastardly behaviour in general. The dice reset to zero after the end of each story, as people begin to look past your good looks. <br /> <br /> Infatuation:<br /> At any point you can attempt to get a person infatuated with you through seduction, which goes above and beyond making a breathtaking first impression. Follow the usual rules for seduction, but the action is an extended one (the ST might allow it to be contested with Self-Control or Intelligence for particularly mismatched couples). You must gain more successes on the attempt than the target's Willpower. If you do so, or if you roleplay it appropriately, the ST can rule you've got them lusting after you. From hereon in, you get to add your whole Appearance as extra dice to subsequent social interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:05:55-07:00","id":993955,"title":"","content":"By the way, if you make Appearance a Background and want to retain the balance of Attributes, you could pop in Composure to replace it.<br /> <br /> I do like Appearance as a determiner of social initiative, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:51:08-07:00","id":994167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=993953#post993953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another option: make Appearance a Background. It doesn't get used much, and charging Attribute costs for it seems unfair as a result. Then give it two main functions: First Impressions and Infatuation.<br /> <br /> First Impressions:<br /> You roll Appearance in appropriate social situations (usually when introducing yourself to a new person), and each success adds a dice to all subsequent social interactions with that person for the remainder of the story. These extra dice can be lost through social faux pas or dastardly behaviour in general. The dice reset to zero after the end of each story, as people begin to look past your good looks.<br /> <br /> Infatuation:<br /> At any point you can attempt to get a person infatuated with you through seduction, which goes above and beyond making a breathtaking first impression. Follow the usual rules for seduction, but the action is an extended one (the ST might allow it to be contested with Self-Control or Intelligence...</div> </div> </div> </div>GURPS stopped basing Will on Intelligence for a good reason. Smart people are never immune to their own bad habits by dint of being smart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You must gain more successes on the attempt than the target's Willpower. If you do so, or if you roleplay it appropriately, the ST can rule you've got them lusting after you. From hereon in, you get to add your whole Appearance as extra dice to subsequent social interactions. </div> </div> </div>It seems like just adopting the social influence system of EX3 would be easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By the way, if you make Appearance a Background and want to retain the balance of Attributes, you could pop in Composure to replace it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I do like Appearance as a determiner of social initiative, though.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Aya Tari basically just suggested that. It doesn't really fit, though, because Appearance doesn't really work like Composure, and we already have the potential to tap Wits for it.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:29:43-07:00","id":994183,"title":"","content":"Actually, the most recent edition of GURPS (4th edition) derives base Will and base Per from IQ, though they can independently raise or lower Will or Per. Mental disadvantages are based on frequency of incident, rather than on Will, which is how they got around high IQ characters abusing the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:37:16-07:00","id":994190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=994183#post994183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the most recent edition of GURPS (4th edition) derives base Will and base Per from IQ, though they can independently raise or lower Will or Per. Mental disadvantages are based on frequency of incident, rather than on Will, which is how they got around high IQ characters abusing the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn I heard otherwise. Ah, well, Int should still not play into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:35:06-07:00","id":994898,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I will keep with the idea I just had, of using Appearance or Charisma based on the &quot;target&quot; being more into behavior or looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T05:19:04-07:00","id":995157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=994167#post994167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> GURPS stopped basing Will on Intelligence for a good reason. Smart people are never immune to their own bad habits by dint of being smart.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It seems like just adopting the social influence system of EX3 would be easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aya Tari basically just suggested that. It doesn't really fit, though, because Appearance doesn't really work like Composure, and we already have the potential to tap Wits for it.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I was agreeing. Emphasis on the could (should've used italics). But I wasn't suggesting Appearance should encompass Composure, but that you cross it out and just replace it. Then you take those functions out of Wits (which makes sense anyway--why should a Mental Attribute offer Social resistance?).<br /> <br /> I agree with Intelligence not equalling Will, but not every critter has Self-Control. Unless you guesstimate it for every non-Vampire character. If Appearance does get swapped out for Composure, you could use that trait, of course<br /> <br /> I'm not saying any of this is a preferable idea. I'm just offering fixes to the OP. I'm never that bothered about Appearance in my games (although I'd be tempted to reduce the costs so it doesn't become a dump stat).<br /> <br /> By the way, what's the social influence system from EX3 like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-29-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:24:55-07:00","id":995186,"title":"","content":"I do not like it because it works as a form of social combat. The way that it uses Appearance is that Appearance grants a die pool bonus to social conflicts equal to the amount that it exceeds the target's Resolve (a derived stat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T22:42:17-08:00","id":1001205,"title":"","content":"I'd like to replace the appearance attribute with a Mien Attribute (Similar to how Requiem has bearing). The Mien attribute will cover how the character presents themselves as well as body language. (Non verbal communication)<br /> <br /> Verbal communication will generally be handled by charisma and manipulation. The concept of appearance (good and bad) will be relegated to Merits and Flaws which will have modifiers to Mien based rolls interacting with certain abilities (good and bad).<br /> <br /> So yes this would mean that Nosferatu and other similarly monstrous Cainites could (and should) invest in the attribute, just their weakness would need to be tweaked with appropriate flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Nothing is free, not even revenge. - Kain; Blood Omen","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1388-ctuncks","name":"ctuncks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T00:01:45-08:00","id":1001230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=992275#post992275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted and Adventure! both share a good idea on that point. It also prevents Nosferatu from gaming their Social Attributes so that they only have to pay for two out of three!</div> </div> </div> </div>A good <i>idea</i> but an overpowered implementation, at least if talking about Exalted 2e: a level of MDV modification is worth approximately two dice, making App twice as good for (non-Surprise) attack and twice as good for all social defenses. At a minimum, the modifier should be reduced to extra dice, and probably restricted to attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=995186#post995186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not like it because it works as a form of social combat. The way that it uses Appearance is that Appearance grants a die pool bonus to social conflicts equal to the amount that it exceeds the target's Resolve (a derived stat).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you only change the die pool when it <i>exceeds</i> a target's stat, then it means that dumping Appearance has no negative effect (you're unlikely to enjoy a bonus with App 2, and lose almost nothing by taking App 1). Instead, the street should go both ways: Hunchback of Notre-Dame de Paris should get his <i>penalty</i> to social interactions for being only mildly less ugly than the Nosferatu, not just be deprived of a bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:09:22-08:00","id":1001421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=1001230#post1001230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good <i>idea</i> but an overpowered implementation, at least if talking about Exalted 2e: a level of MDV modification is worth approximately two dice, making App twice as good for (non-Surprise) attack and twice as good for all social defenses. At a minimum, the modifier should be reduced to extra dice, and probably restricted to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've moved on to third edition, so any entreaty to talk about second is not going to be heeded.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:37:03-08:00","id":1001658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=1001421#post1001421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've moved on to third edition, so any entreaty to talk about second is not going to be heeded.</div> </div> </div> </div>My second paragraph seems to contain criticism applicable to 3e, as far as I remember how 3e works. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T15:38:43-08:00","id":1001956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991835-making-appearance-work-for-you?p=1001658#post1001658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My second paragraph seems to contain criticism applicable to 3e, as far as I remember how 3e works. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also addressed to someone else, and I wasn't following that conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}